  "problem": "Which of the following $x$-values is in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254348/assets/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nThe domain of the function contains all real numbers except for $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…$ \n\nOf the given values, the only one that lies in the domain is $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{5}.$",
